### Authentication API Tests
### You can use this file with VS Code REST Client extension or similar tools

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@contentType = application/json

### ============================================
### SIGNUP TESTS
### ============================================

### Test 1: Successful Registration
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "first_name": "John",
  "last_name": "Doe",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### Test 2: Registration with Missing Fields
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "first_name": "Jane",
  "email": "jane@example.com"
}

### Test 3: Registration with Invalid Email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "first_name": "Bob",
  "last_name": "Smith",
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### Test 4: Registration with Weak Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "first_name": "Alice",
  "last_name": "Johnson",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "weak"
}

### Test 5: Registration with Short Names
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "first_name": "A",
  "last_name": "B",
  "email": "ab@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### Test 6: Registration with Special Characters in Name
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "first_name": "Mary-Jane",
  "last_name": "O'Connor",
  "email": "mary.jane@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### Test 7: Duplicate Email Registration
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "first_name": "John",
  "last_name": "Duplicate",
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### ============================================
### LOGIN TESTS
### ============================================

### Test 8: Successful Login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### Test 9: Login with Wrong Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword123"
}

### Test 10: Login with Non-existent Email
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "notfound@example.com",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### Test 11: Login with Missing Password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com"
}

### Test 12: Login with Invalid Email Format
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password": "SecurePass123"
}

### ============================================
### AUTHENTICATED ENDPOINT TEST
### ============================================

### Test 13: Access Protected Route (Replace TOKEN with actual token from login)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

### Test 14: Access Protected Route without Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/profile
